{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>For his brother, etc., and he alone.</b> That is, he comes to give a reason for why he is anxious about the doubtful danger to Binyamin more than the certain fate of Shimon, who is imprisoned in the guard of Egypt under pledge, and when they do not bring Binyamin, behold he is liable to death. Therefore he said: for this one must be insistent, for his brother is dead — which did not happen to any of the other brothers; and moreover, his loss is not like the loss of Shimon, for he alone remains solitary to his mother, which is not so with Shimon, who has five brothers. Furthermore, this doubt is a decisively outweighed doubt, and so it is when he says <b>and harm will befall him</b> — and he did not say ״if harm befalls him״ etc. And he was precise to say <b>on the road that you travel</b>: he alluded that Yosef his brother traveled on the road they are accustomed to travel continually from Chevron to Shechem, and even so he was surely torn; and likewise, this — one must fear for harm to him even on the road that you travel on continually without any apprehension."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:12.440321823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}